      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Our Craft",
        "title_l1": "Every stitch carries",
        "title_l2": "a signature",
        "copy": "<p>Shrujan began in 1969 with Chanda Shroff, known as Kaki, who went to Kutch after a famine and found women whose embroidery was extraordinary and whose earnings were not. She turned that skill into a livelihood.</p><p>From her vision to the hands of thousands of women across Kutch, Shrujan has quietly safeguarded the region’s living craft traditions for over five decades, preserving the knowledge and the dignity behind it.</p>",
        "link_label": "Explore the Craft",
